# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=flash
Version=v1.0.0_H5_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
advanced_settings|Activate|Advanced settings||||<font color="red"><b>By enabling this feature, you have access to risky settings that could be harmful for your device.</b></font>
OB_Product_State_active|Activate|Product State||||Product states to protect memory content from debug access. Open: User Flash open (TZ secure and non-secure open) External access (debug) N and NS enabled (~RDP0). Provisioning: Provisioning - immutable root of trust is being installed. nv-Open if TZEN is disabled. iROT-provisioned: The immutable root of trust is installed. (~RDP 0.5). TZ-Closed: State for debugging the NS application. Debug is restrained to non-secure areas. Closed: State for running a secure application. Debug disabled, regression is possible. Locked: Transition to other state, policy change or debug is not permitted. Regression: The temporary state initiated by the debug authentication system in transition to nv-Open. NS-Regression: The temporary state initiated by the debug authentication system in transition to nv-Closed_secure.
OB_ProductState|Product state|Product State||||
ProductState|Product state|Product State||||
OB_BOR_Level_active|Activate|BOR Level||||
OB_BOR_level|BOR Level|BOR Level||||<font color="green">Bits 1:0 </font> <b>BOR_LEV[1:0]: </b>Brownout level option status bit These bits reflects the power level that generates a system reset. 00: BOR OFF, POR/PDR reset threshold level is applied 01: BOR Level 1, the threshold level is low (around 2.1 V) 10: BOR Level 2, the threshold level is medium (around 2.4 V) 11: BOR Level 3, the threshold level is high (around 2.7 V)
OB_BORH|BORH_EN|BOR Level||||<font color="green">Bit 2 </font> <b>BORH_EN:</b> Brownout high enable 0: disable 1: enable
OB_User_Configuration_active|Activate|User Configuration||||
USERConfig|USERConfig1|||||
OB_IO_VDD_HSLV_UI|IO_VDD_HSLV|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 16</font> <b> IO_VDD_HSLV:</b> High-speed IO at low VDD voltage configuration bit. This bit can be set only with VDD below 2.7 V. 0: High-speed IO at low VDD voltage feature disabled (VDD can exceed 2.7 V). 1: High-speed IO at low VDD voltage feature enabled (VDD remains below 2.7 V).
OB_IO_VDD_HSLV|IO_VDD_HSLV|User Configuration||||
OB_IO_VDDIO2_HSLV_UI|IO_VDDIO2_HSLV|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 17</font> <b> IO_VDDIO2_HSLV:</b> High-speed IO at low VDDIO2 voltage configuration bit. This bit can be set only with VDDIO2 below 2.7 V. 0: High-speed IO at low VDDIO2 voltage feature disabled (VDDIO2 can exceed 2.7 V). 1: High-speed IO at low VDDIO2 voltage feature enabled (VDDIO2 remains below 2.7 V).
OB_IO_VDDIO2_HSLV|IO_VDDIO2_HSLV|User Configuration||||
OB_IWDG_STOP_UI|IWDG_STOP|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 20 </font> <b>IWDG_STOP:</b> IWDG Stop mode freeze option configuration bit. When set the independent watchdog IWDG is in system Stop mode. Disable: Independent watchdog frozen in system Stop mode. Enable: Independent watchdog keep running in system Stop mode.
OB_IWDG_STOP|IWDG_STOP|User Configuration||||
OB_IWDG_STDBY_UI|IWDG_STDBY|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 21 </font> <b>IWDG_STDBY:</b> IWDG Standby mode freeze option configuration bit. When set the independent watchdog IWDG is frozen in system Standby mode. Disable: Independent watchdog frozen in Standby mode. Enable: Independent watchdog keep running in Standby mode.
OB_IWDG_STDBY|IWDG_STDBY|User Configuration||||
OB_BOOT_UBE_UI|BOOT_UBE|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 29:22 </font> <b>SWAP_BANK [7:0]:</b>Unique boot entry control, selects either ST or OEM iRoT for secure boot. This information is also used by RSS to boot through ST-iROT when in Open PRODUCT_STATE. <font color="red">Can only be changed in product states open for debug like Open and also in Provisioning. SECBOOT_LOCK must be disabled to change.</font> OEM-iRoT: User Flash selected. ST-iRoT: System Flash selected.
OB_BOOT_UBE|BOOT_UBE|User Configuration||||
OB_SWAP_BANK_UI|SWAP_BANK|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 2Unchecked </font> <b>SWAP_BANK:</b> Swap banks. SWAP_BANK option bit is used to configure whether the Bank1 and Bank2 are swapped or not. This bit is loaded with the SWAP_BANK bit of FLASH_OPTSR_CUR register after a reset. Disable: Bank1 and Bank2 not swapped. Enable: Bank 1 and bank 2 swapped.
OB_SWAP_BANK|SWAP_BANK|User Configuration||||
OB_IWDG_SW_UI|IWDG_SW|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 3 </font> <b>IWDG_SW: </b>: IWDG control mode option configuration bit. Disable: IWDG watchdog is controlled by hardware. Enable: IWDG watchdog is controlled by software.
OB_IWDGSW|IWDG_SW|User Configuration||||
OB_WWDG_SW_UI|WWDG_SW|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 4 </font> <b>WWDG_SW:</b> WWDG control mode option configuraton bit. Disable: WWDG watchdog is controlled by hardware. Enable: WWDG watchdog is controlled by software.
OB_WWDGSW|WWDG_SW|User Configuration||||
OB_NRST_STOP_UI|nRST_STOP|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 6 </font> <b>nRST_STOP:</b> Core domain Stop entry reset option configuration bit. Disable: A reset is generated when entering Stop mode on core domain. Enable: No reset generated when entering Stop mode on core domain.
OB_nRST_STOP|nRST_STOP|User Configuration||||
OB_NRST_STDBY_UI|nRST_STDBY|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 7 </font> <b>nRST_STDBY:</b> Core domain Standby entry reset option configuration bit. Disable: A reset is generated when entering Standby mode on core domain. Enable: No reset generated when entering Standby mode on core domain.
OB_nRST_STDBY|nRST_STDBY|User Configuration||||
USERConfig2|USERConfig2|||||
OB_User_Configuration2_active|Activate|User Configuration 2||||
OB_TZEN|TZEN|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 31:24</font> <b> TZEN[7:0]:</b> Trust Zone enable configuration bits. This bit enables the device is in trust zone mode during an option byte change. OB_TZEN_DISABLE:0xC3: Trust zone disabled. OB_TZEN_ENABLE:0xB4: Trust zone enabled. <font color="red">This Option byte cannot be set throught CubeMX</font>
OB_SRAM1_ECC_UI|SRAM1_ECC|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 10 </font> <b>SRAM2_ECC: </b> SRAM1 ECC detection and correction disable. Enable: SRAM2 ECC check enabled. Disable: SRAM2 ECC check disabled.
OB_SRAM1_ECC|SRAM1_ECC|User Configuration 2||||
OB_SRAM1_RST_UI|SRAM1_RST|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 9 </font> <b>SRAM1_RST: </b> SRAM1 erase upon system reset. Disable: SRAM1 erased when a system reset occurs. Enable: SRAM1 not erased when a system reset occurs.
OB_SRAM1_RST|SRAM1_RST|User Configuration2||||
OB_SRAM2_ECC_UI|SRAM2_ECC|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 6 </font> <b>SRAM2_ECC: </b> SRAM2 ECC detection and correction disable. Enable: SRAM2 ECC check enabled. Disable: SRAM2 ECC check disabled.
OB_SRAM2_ECC|SRAM2_ECC|User Configuration 2||||
OB_SRAM2_RST_UI|SRAM2_RST|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 3 </font> <b>SRAM2_RST: </b> SRAM2 erase when system reset. Disable: SRAM2 erased when a system reset occurs. Enable: SRAM2 not erased when a system reset occurs.
OB_SRAM2_RST|SRAM2_RST|User Configuration2||||
OB_SRAM3_ECC_UI|SRAM3_ECC|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 5 </font> <b>SRAM3_ECC: </b> SRAM3 ECC detection and correction disable. Enable: SRAM3 ECC check enabled. Disable: SRAM3 ECC check disabled.
OB_SRAM3_ECC|SRAM3_ECC|User Configuration 2||||
OB_SRAM13_RST_UI|SRAM13_RST|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 2 </font> <b>SRAM13_RST: </b> SRAM1 and SRAM3 erase upon system reset. Disable: SRAM1 and SRAM3 erased when a system reset occurs. Enable: SRAM1 and SRAM3 not erased when a system reset occurs.
OB_SRAM13_RST|SRAM13_RST|User Configuration2||||
OB_SRAM1345_RST_UI|SRAM1345_RST|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 2 </font> <b>SRAM13_RST: </b> SRAM1, SRAM3, SRAM4 and SRAM5 erase upon system reset. Disable: SRAM1, SRAM3, SRAM4 and SRAM5 erased when a system reset occurs. Enable: SRAM1, SRAM3, SRAM4 and SRAM5 not erased when a system reset occurs.
OB_SRAM1345_RST|SRAM1345_RST|User Configuration2||||
OB_BKPRAM_ECC_UI|BKPRAM_ECC|User Configuration 2||||<font color="green">Bit 4 </font> <b>BKPRAM_ECC: </b> Backup RAM ECC detection and correction disable. Enable: BKPRAM ECC check enabled. Disable: BKPRAM ECC check disabled.
OB_BKPRAM_ECC|BKPRAM_ECC|User Configuration 2||||
UserConfigCondition|UserConfig_Condition|||||
