OB_Boot_Configuration_active_NS_ADDR|Activate NS BOOT ADDRESS|Boot Configuration||||
OB_NSBOOTADD_Address|Address|Boot Configuration||0x00|0xFFFFFF00|<font color="green">Bit 31:8</font> <b> NSBOOTADD[23:0]:</b>Unique boot entry address. These bits reflect the Secure UBE address.
OB_Boot_Configuration_active_NS_BOOTLOCK|Activate NS BOOT LOCK|Boot Configuration||||
OB_NSBootLock|NSBOOT_LOCK|Boot Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 7:0</font> <b> NSBOOT_LOCK[7:0]:</b> Non secure Boot lock. A field locking the values of SWAP_BANK, and NSBOOTADD settings. Disable: The SWAP_BANK and NSBOOTADD can still be modified following their individual rules. Enable: The NSBOOTADD and SWAP_BANK are frozen.
OB_Boot_Configuration_active_SEC_ADDR|Activate SEC BOOT ADDRESS|Boot Configuration||||
OB_SECBOOTADD_Address|Address|Boot Configuration||0x00|0xFFFFFF00|<font color="green">Bit 31:8</font> <b> SECBOOTADD[23:0]:</b>Unique boot entry address. These bits reflect the Secure UBE address.
OB_Boot_Configuration_active_SEC_BOOTLOCK|Activate SEC BOOT LOCK|Boot Configuration||||
OB_SECBootLock|SECBOOT_LOCK|Boot Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 7:0</font> <b> NSBOOT_LOCK[7:0]:</b> Non secure Boot lock. A field locking the values of SWAP_BANK, and NSBOOTADD settings. Disable: The SWAP_BANK and NSBOOTADD can still be modified following their individual rules. Enable: The NSBOOTADD and SWAP_BANK are frozen.
OB_Bank1_WM_active|Activate Bank1 WM|Flash watermark area definition||||
WMSecStartSector_Bank1|WMSEC Start sector|Flash watermark area definition||0|=numberOfSectors-1|<font color="green">Bit 6:0</font> <b> SECWM1_STRT[6:0]:</b> Bank1 security WM area 1 start sector.
WMSecEndSector_Bank1|WMSEC End sector|Flash watermark area definition||0|=numberOfSectors-1|<font color="green">Bit 22:16</font> <b> SECWM1_END[6:0]:</b> Bank1 security WM area 1 end sector
OB_WMSEC_BOTHBANKS|same WMSEC1 and WMSEC1 for both banks|Flash watermark area definition||||
OB_Bank2_WM_active|Activate Bank2 WM|Flash watermark area definition||||
WMSecStartSector_Bank2|WMSEC Start sector|Flash watermark area definition||0|=numberOfSectors-1|<font color="green">Bit 6:0</font> <b> SECWM1_END[6:0]:</b> This field contains the first page of the secure area in bank 2.
WMSecEndSector_Bank2|WMSEC End sector|Flash watermark area definition||0|=numberOfSectors-1|<font color="green">Bit 22:16</font> <b> SECWM1_END[6:0]:</b> This field contains the first page of the secure area in bank 2.
OB_WRP1_active|Activate Bank 1 WRP|Write sector group Protection||||<font color="green">Bits 7:0 </font> <b>WRPSG1[7:0]: </b> Bank1 sector protection option status byte Setting WRPSG1 bits to 0 write protects the corresponding sectors in bank 1 (0: write protected; 1: not write protected)
