OB_OTP_LOCK_active|Activate|OTP write protection||||<font color="green">Bits 31:0 </font> <b>LOCKBL[31:0]: </b> OTP block lock. Block n corresponds to OTP 16-bit word 32 x n to 32 x n + 31. LOCKBL[n] = 1 indicates that all OTP 16-bit words in OTP Block n are locked and attempt to program them results in WRPERR. LOCKBL[n] = 0 indicates that all OTP 16-bit words in OTP Block n are not locked. When one block is locked, it is not possible to remove the write protection. LOCKBL bits can be set if the corresponding bit in FLASH_OTPBLR_CUR is cleared
